<title>CHILE: DCR downgrades Chile's Edelnor rating.</title>
<headline>DCR downgrades Chile's Edelnor rating.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duff &amp; Phelps Credit Rating Co said it has downgraded its rating of Chilean power utility Edelnor's senior Particpation certificates to BBB minus from BBB, citing pressure on power prices in northern Chile.</p>
<p>The lower rating reflects rising competition in the sector and the possible fall in electricity prices in the nothern grid as the result of the start-up of gas-fired plants in coming years, said the statement.</p>
<p>Edelnor, one of Chile's smaller power generators, is 65-percent owned by U.S. firm Southern Co.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
